{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Will a man of a hundred years be born.</b> He marvels because the seed of an old man is cold, therefore he cannot beget. And the greater wonder is how a woman whose blood has ceased can give birth. For from blood the son is built and established. And when you look and see, you find that Sarah's matter is more wondrous than Abraham's, for behold, we have found fathers who each begot a son when he was older than ninety years, and the lives of the generations in Abraham's time are longer than the life of one generation, and as soon as the angel departed he immediately circumcised his son and every one born in his house and bought with his money."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:54.595622087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}